  "unreadable": [],
  "uncertain": [
    "Image 1 Qwiic connector: the callout text under the inset reads 'GND 3V3 14 13' but the board silkscreen at the pins reads '3V3 GND 14 13' (left to right); I used the silkscreen (positions 3 = GND, 4 = 3V3 from the USB end). Image 2's callout '3V3 GND 14 13' agrees with the silkscreen."
  ],
  "notes": "Callout lists are grouped in two blocks per side; matched to the inner/outer hole columns by the board-photo silkscreen in the same image. Name-box spellings (08, 05, 09, 3-1, 12-1, CLK...) kept as first function; photo silkscreen prints 8, 5, 9 without leading zero. Image 1 adds GPIO39/GPIO42/GPIO40/GPIO41 beside TCK/TMS/TDO/TDI; image 2 (titled T7_S3 V1.1) prints only the JTAG names. Skipped JST-GH 1.25mm battery connector (only +/- marks), USB Type-C, Reset, Boot, power switch, LEDs."
}